      "content": "The \"logic\" of supporting the climate act is that silence on existential threats is a liability, not a neutral position, and modern consumers view corporate neutrality on climate as complicity in inaction. While older demographics might prefer traditional stability, they are increasingly becoming a minority of the purchasing power that drives market trends, and alienating them now is a gamble with a very high cost. A formal statement of support positions your company as a responsible leader who understands that long-term survival depends on addressing climate change, whereas neutrality is a short-term tactic that will be remembered as cowardice by the public.",
